MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A fresh-context hostile reviewer attacked the self-sufficiency
mechanisms; the spec's new ADVERSARIAL REVIEW 2026-08-23 section records
every finding, acted or deliberately not.

Acted (each with a regression test; mutations RED -> byte-identical
restore -> GREEN):
- K1 port-less server = unverifiable, never killable (was the one
  unverifiable condition that failed toward killing)
- K2 TOCTOU: kill path re-verifies /proc starttime captured at
  evaluation; mismatch = identity_changed, no signal
- K4 two-cycle dead confirmation before janitor auto-start, plus
  scripts/conductor-stop.sh (hold-then-stop, no window)
- S1 import failure writes the receipt WITH the failure note
- S2 temp-dir server-log fallback restored (sentinel parity)
- S3 parsed-but-zero-rows counts as the no-rows shape
- N2 packets at first sighting while disarmed; packet states arming is
  GLOBAL and standing
- N5 REAPED is only written when a signal landed; EPERM gets its own row
- S5 janitor runs the findings ledger (aging no longer depends on
  milestone closes)
- SIGKILL-after-grace branch now under test

Deliberately not acted, recorded in the spec appendix: discovery breadth
(python -m / Kaggle kernel / vLLM invisible to sentinel and authority
alike — needs its own corpus sweep per rule 5; vLLM orphans stay
human-handled), remote-port false dead-port evidence (bounded by the
rows conjunction and the disarmed default), FRESHEXEC dirty-tree
silence, orphaned children of a stopped run.

